</text><rect x=\"36\" y=\"360\" width=\"140\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b3bbc8\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"48\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2433\">App B</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#5d6575\">Testing</text><rect x=\"196\" y=\"360\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#eef2fd\" stroke=\"#6f88e3\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"208\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2a5c\">agent/B-7</text><text x=\"208\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#4d5884\">PR #58</text><path d=\"M373,384 L393,384\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"393\" y=\"360\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#3d5cd6\" stroke=\"#3d5cd6\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"405\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#ffffff\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Check · Review</text><text x=\"405\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dbe2fb\" textLength=\"94\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">CI + another model</text><path d=\"M570,384 L590,384\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"590\" y=\"360\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c3cad6\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"></rect><text x=\"602\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#6b7383\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Accept · Merge</text><text x=\"602\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#8a92a0\" textLength=\"84\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Verify in preview</text><path d=\"M767,384 L787,384\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"787\" y=\"360\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c3cad6\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"></rect><text x=\"799\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#6b7383\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Staging → Production</text><text x=\"799\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#8a92a0\" textLength=\"60\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Approval required</text><rect x=\"36\" y=\"422\" width=\"140\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b3bbc8\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"48\" y=\"443\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2433\">App C</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"461\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#5d6575\" textLength=\"48\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Deploying</text><rect x=\"196\" y=\"422\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#eef2fd\" stroke=\"#6f88e3\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"208\" y=\"443\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2a5c\">agent/C-3</text><text x=\"208\" y=\"461\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#4d5884\">PR #12</text><path d=\"M373,446 L393,446\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"393\" y=\"422\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#eef2fd\" stroke=\"#6f88e3\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"405\" y=\"443\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2a5c\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Check · Review</text><text x=\"405\" y=\"461\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#4d5884\" textLength=\"94\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">CI + another model</text><path d=\"M570,446 L590,446\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"590\" y=\"422\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#eef2fd\" stroke=\"#6f88e3\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"602\" y=\"443\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1f2a5c\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Accept · Merge</text><text x=\"602\" y=\"461\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#4d5884\" textLength=\"84\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Verify in preview</text><path d=\"M767,446 L787,446\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><rect x=\"787\" y=\"422\" width=\"177\" height=\"48\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#3d5cd6\" stroke=\"#3d5cd6\" stroke-width=\"1\"></rect><text x=\"799\" y=\"443\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#ffffff\" textLength=\"77\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Staging → Production</text><text x=\"799\" y=\"461\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dbe2fb\" textLength=\"60\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Approval required</text><path d=\"M875.5,470 L875.5,488 L284.5,488 L284.5,470\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a8291\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#d4-a)\"></path><text x=\"580\" y=\"506\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#4a5160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" textLength=\"115\" lengthAdjust=\"spacingAndGlyphs\">Repeat for the next change</text></svg></div>\n        <ul class=\"fit\">\n          <li><b><i class=\"st ok\"></i>Each application moves at its own pace</b>One application can be in development while another is deploying, without blocking each other.</li>\n          <li><b><i class=\"st ok\"></i>Every change is tested</b>Run CI checks, review with another model, then deploy to a preview environment dedicated to the PR.</li>\n          <li><b><i class=\"st ok\"></i>Controlled releases</b>Merge after human acceptance. Staging deploys automatically; production requires another person's approval and supports rollback.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- 04 -->\n  <section class=\"sec\" id=\"s5\">\n    <p class=\"label\">04</p>\n    <h2>Why choose NocoBase 3</h2>\n    <p class=\"lead\">For AI-built business systems, NocoBase 3 provides a stronger starting point and more reliable delivery.</p>\n    <div class=\"sec-body\">\n      <div class=\"why\">\n        <div>\n          <span class=\"vs\">Compared with building from scratch</span>\n          <h3>The foundations are ready</h3>\n          <p>Authentication, permissions, state machines, notifications, files, databases, localization, and deployment tools are ready. AI focuses on business logic instead of rebuilding the foundations for every project.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <span class=\"vs\">Compared with other frameworks</span>\n          <h3>Business capabilities are packaged</h3>\n          <p>More than a technical framework: permission sets, sharing and restriction rules, approvals, inboxes, Agents, and business components for sign-in, boards, and diagrams are ready to use.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <span class=\"vs\">Compared with ready-made solutions</span>\n          <h3>Ready to use and customize</h3>\n          <p>Solutions such as CRM and ERP work out of the box, support private deployment, and provide full source code for AI to extend around your business.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"exp\">\n        <h3>Built on experience serving NocoBase 2 customers</h3>\n        <p>Businesses, governments, and universities worldwide use NocoBase 2 to build business systems. This experience informs NocoBase 3 capabilities and Solutions.</p>\n        <img class=\"logos\" src=\"/architecture-pitch/image-4.jpeg\" alt=\"NocoBase customer logos: ISUZU, YAMAHA, SONY, NXP, Lenovo, BOE, DAIKIN, Bank of China, Peking University, and more\">\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- 05 -->\n  <section class=\"sec\" id=\"s4\">\n    <p class=\"label\">05</p>\n    <h2>Comparison</h2>\n    <p class=\"lead\">Compare how the three approaches address common concerns.</p>\n    <div class=\"sec-body cmp\">\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Where business logic lives</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><span class=\"kind cfg\">Configuration</span>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Tables, pages, permissions, and workflows are database configuration, read and executed by the platform.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><span class=\"kind mix\">Configuration + source</span>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>Pages become React source; APIs, schemas, permissions, and workflows remain configuration.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><span class=\"kind src\">Source code</span>NocoBase 3</span><p>Everything lives in your code repository. NocoBase is used only through dependencies:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>client/</b>: pages, routes, and layouts with React · Vite</li>\n              <li><b>server/</b>: APIs, services, and permission rules with Hono</li>\n              <li><b>database/</b>: schema migrations and seed data</li>\n              <li><b>Dependencies</b>: framework, capability packages, and libraries</li>\n              <li><b>Business components</b>: copy source from UI Library into your project</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Independent development and modular releases</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st no\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>All modules share configuration in one database. Migrations select by table, making it difficult to release a single module.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st part\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>Frontends can be developed and deployed independently; the backend configuration issues remain.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>Each module is developed on its own branch. Release what you merge:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Branch development</b>: one branch and one PR per task</li>\n              <li><b>Automated checks</b>: CI runs linting, type checks, and tests</li>\n              <li><b>Preview acceptance</b>: a dedicated preview environment for each PR</li>\n              <li><b>Release merged changes</b>: unfinished work stays on branches without affecting releases</li>\n              <li><b>Multiple applications</b>: Studio manages each application's environments and releases</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Workflows</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st no\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Visual configuration offers many nodes and versioning, but complex flows are difficult and inflexible to configure, and changes cannot be reviewed like code.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st no\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>The same as NocoBase 2: still configuration.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>Describe business processes as state machines in code:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>States and transitions</b>: each record stores its current state and transitions according to rules.</li>\n              <li><b>Triggers</b>: automatically handle a record when its time in a state exceeds a timeout.</li>\n              <li><b>Side effects</b>: execute after commit with retries and idempotency; continue transitions after success or failure.</li>\n              <li><b>Waiting</b>: wait for human actions, external callbacks, or polling results.</li>\n              <li><b>Recovery</b>: resume unfinished work after a service restart.</li>\n            </ul>\n            <p class=\"note\">The approval plugin provides multilevel approvals, countersigning, and additional approvers.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Permissions</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st no\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Roles, data scopes, and field permissions are configurable, but complex rules are difficult to configure and changes are hard to review.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st no\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>The same as NocoBase 2: still configuration.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>Rules are written in code; assignments are managed centrally in the application:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Permission sets</b>: similar to roles, assigned to users or teams.</li>\n              <li><b>Record level</b>: records I own, records I created, or custom conditions.</li>\n              <li><b>Field level</b>: separate control over readable and writable fields.</li>\n              <li><b>Default access</b>: broaden the scope for everyone with permission to perform the action.</li>\n              <li><b>Sharing</b>: broaden the scope for specific people or teams.</li>\n              <li><b>Restrictions</b>: narrow the scope regardless of where permission comes from.</li>\n              <li><b>Permission origins</b>: explain where a permission comes from.</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Multiple applications, shared data</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Multiple entry points in one application share data directly. Across applications, an External NocoBase data source can read and write another application's data.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>Multiple Portals within the same application share data directly.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>One application maintains master data; others connect to it:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Primary database</b>: SQLite, PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server, Oracle, Dameng, KingbaseES, OceanBase</li>\n              <li><b>External data sources</b>: connect databases from other applications or existing systems</li>\n              <li><b>Read/write scope</b>: read-only access, or write access to selected tables and fields</li>\n              <li><b>Access permissions</b>: enforced on the server</li>\n              <li><b>Synchronization</b>: write synchronization tasks when needed</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Integrating existing systems</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st part\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Call external APIs through workflow HTTP request nodes; complex integrations are limited by node capabilities.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st part\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>The same as NocoBase 2.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>Write integration logic directly in code:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Call external APIs</b>: use state machine side effects with retries and idempotency</li>\n              <li><b>Receive callbacks</b>: define your own API routes</li>\n              <li><b>Scheduled tasks</b>: scheduling, queues, and background jobs</li>\n              <li><b>External databases</b>: connect as external data sources</li>\n              <li><b>Expose APIs</b>: access business APIs using API keys</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>AI-assisted business operations</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st part\"></i>NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>AI employees embedded in pages help users query data, fill forms, and analyze content. Local Agents can call APIs through nb api, but these are generic API calls.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st part\"></i>NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>The same as NocoBase 2.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\"><i class=\"st ok\"></i>NocoBase 3</span><p>The agents plugin connects to both models and runners:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Online Agents</b>: connect directly to models, run on the server, and use the application's business commands as tools</li>\n              <li><b>Worker Agents</b>: drive Claude Code, Codex, and other tools on runners</li>\n              <li><b>Application-specific CLI</b>: package business APIs into a CLI in one step for users' local Agents</li>\n              <li><b>The user's own permissions</b>: after CLI sign-in, execute with the user's permissions</li>\n              <li><b>Records</b>: inspect conversations, run records, and usage</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topic\">\n        <h3>Version control and delivery</h3>\n        <div class=\"cells\">\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\">NocoBase 2 No-code</span><p>Version snapshots, backup and restore, and migration-based releases.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\">NocoBase 2 AI Portal</span><p>Frontend source can be stored in Git and pushed and deployed with nb portal.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"cell\"><span class=\"who\">NocoBase 3</span><p>Manage and deliver it like conventional software:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><b>Git</b>: version the entire project and review code</li>\n              <li><b>CI/CD</b>: use any platform to build a deployment archive</li>\n              <li><b>Deployment</b>: deploy locally with app-installer, or over SSH to an offline Linux server</li>\n              <li><b>Upgrades and rollbacks</b>: handled by app-installer</li>\n              <li><b>Containers</b>: templates include a Dockerfile</li>\n            </ul></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"keys\"><span><i class=\"st ok\"></i>Supported</span><span><i class=\"st part\"></i>Partially supported</span><span><i class=\"st no\"></i>Not supported</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n</main>"
